  "id": "BIT-postgresql-2026-116318",
  "summary": "PostgreSQL pg_dump not-null constraint name allows SQL injection",
  "details": "SQL injection in PostgreSQL pg_dump allows an object creator to execute arbitrary SQL as the user restoring the dump, via an inherited column having a child-local not-null constraint whose name requires quoting.  Within major version 18, minor versions before PostgreSQL 18.7 are affected.  Versions before PostgreSQL 18 are unaffected.",
